#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:2
msgid "Work with groups, filter, and sort"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-ent.rst:9
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry, Enterprise, and Enterprise "
"Advanced plans <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ (not available on "
"Professional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:7
msgid ""
"Your board can be grouped, filtered, and sorted into different views "
"using a range of properties. This gives you a powerful way to track work "
"from various perspectives. When used in conjunction with :ref:`saved "
"views <end-user-guide/project-management/work-with-views:work with saved "
"views>`, you can create multiple views with different groupings and "
"filters for quick access without having to reapply the groupings and "
"filters every time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:9
msgid ""
"For example, easily find tasks assigned to you or a team member using the"
" person or multi-person filters, and keep track of upcoming tasks with "
"date filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:12
msgid "Group cards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:14
msgid ""
"You can group cards on your board if they utilize the **Select** or "
"**Person** property. Card grouping is only available in board and table "
"views and you must have at least one **Select** or **Person** property on"
" your board for grouping to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:17
msgid "Apply a group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:19
msgid ""
"To apply a group, select the **Group by** option at the top of the board,"
" then select any available **Select** or **Person** property to group "
"your cards by."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:21
msgid ""
"In the :ref:`boards view <end-user-guide/project-management/work-with-"
"views:board view>`, cards are automatically grouped into columns by the "
"values from the specified property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:22
msgid ""
"In the `table view <end-user-guide/project-management/work-with-"
"views:board view>`, grouped cards will appear in individual sections "
"based on the values from the specified property. Select the arrow to the "
"left of the group name to expand or collapse cards in the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:25
msgid "Hide and unhide groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:27
msgid ""
"To hide a group, select the options menu **(...)** to the right of any "
"group name, then select **Hide**. Additionally, in table view only, you "
"can hide empty groups by selecting the **Group by** option at the top of "
"the board, then selecting **Hide empty groups**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:28
msgid ""
"To unhide a group, go to the hidden column section towards the right of a"
" board view, select the group you want to unhide, then select **Show**. "
"On table view, select the **Group by** option at the top of the board, "
"then select **Show hidden groups**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:31
msgid "Ungroup cards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:33
msgid ""
"To ungroup cards on table view, select the **Group by** option at the top"
" of the board, then select **Ungroup** from the top of the menu. This "
"will return your table to its default state. Cards can be ungrouped in "
"table view only. Ungrouping is not possible on board view since groups "
"are used to determine what to display."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:36
msgid "Filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:38
msgid ""
"You can filter cards on your board if they utilize any of the following "
"property types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:40
msgid "Select"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:41
msgid "Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:42
msgid "Email"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:43
msgid "Phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:44
msgid "URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:45
msgid "Date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:46
msgid "Person"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:47
msgid "Multi-person"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:48
msgid "Created time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:49
msgid "Created by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:50
msgid "Last updated time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:51
msgid "Last updated by"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:53
msgid ""
"To use filters, you must have the above property types already added to "
"your board. Go to **Filter > Add filter**, and select the property you "
"wish to filter by. You can use the modifiers to get even more granular "
"results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:56
msgid "Add filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:58
msgid ""
"To add a filter, select the **Filter** option at the top of the board, "
"then select **+ Add filter**. To change the property to filter by, select"
" the name of the first property, then select another property (if "
"available) from the menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:60
msgid "**Specify the filtering criteria**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:62
msgid "**Includes**: Display cards with any of the specified values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:63
msgid ""
"**Doesn’t include**: Display all cards without any of the specified "
"values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:64
msgid "**Is empty**: Display cards with no values assigned to a property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:65
msgid "**Is not empty**: Display cards with any value assigned to a property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:67
msgid ""
"To add another filtering layer, repeat the steps above with another "
"property to refine your filtering results. Adding another layer will "
"display cards that only match the criteria from the first layer and the "
"second layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:70
msgid "Delete filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:72
msgid ""
"To delete a filter, select the **Filter** option at the top of the board,"
" then select **Delete** to the right of each filtering layer. Delete all "
"filtering layers to completely remove filters from the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:75
msgid "Sorting cards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:77
msgid ""
"Cards can be sorted by the card name or by any property available on the "
"card."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:81
msgid "Sorting is only available in boards, table, and gallery views."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:84
msgid "Apply sorting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:86
msgid ""
"To apply a sort, select the **Sort** option at the top of the board, then"
" select an option from the menu. The cards will be sorted in ascending "
"order by default based on the selected option and the **Sort** menu will "
"display an upward pointing arrow next to the selected option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:88
msgid ""
"To change the sort order to descending order, select the same option "
"again from the **Sort** menu. The cards will now be sorted in descending "
"order and the menu will display a downward pointing arrow next to the "
"selected option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:91
msgid "Clear sorting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/project-management/groups-filter-sort.rst:93
msgid ""
"To clear a sort, select the **Sort** option at the top of the board, then"
" select the **Manual** option from the top of the menu."
msgstr ""

